# Environment
@hosturl = http://localhost:4000
@authToken =
@xTenantId = local
@xBranchId = test
@uploadUrl = PASTE_data.upload_FROM_SSS_URL

### 1. Sss Url Public
# `type` is mandatory — appended to the object key. `provider` is derived
# server-side from x-tenant-id/x-branch-id headers (each defaults to "admin").
GET {{hosturl}}/sss-url?fileName=JetBrainMonoFont.png&type=Test-Application
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
x-tenant-id: {{xTenantId}}
x-branch-id: {{xBranchId}}

### 2. Sss Url Private
GET {{hosturl}}/sss-url?fileName=jwt.png&private=true&type=Profile%20Photos
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
x-tenant-id: {{xTenantId}}
x-branch-id: {{xBranchId}}

### 3. Sss Put Upload
# PUT the file bytes to the signed upload URL from GET /sss-url (data.upload).
# Do not send Authorization or Content-Type — the signature only includes host.
# This URL expires in 300s; paste a fresh data.upload if you get 403.
PUT {{uploadUrl}}

# Replace with the file to upload
< ./file.png
